.Dd October 23, 2026
.Dt IEEE80211_IOCTL 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ieee80211_cfgget , ieee80211_cfgset , ieee80211_ioctl ,
.Nm ieee80211_ioctl_sae , ieee80211_sta_request_validate
.Nd 802.11 interface ioctl commands
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In net80211/ieee80211_var.h
.In net80211/ieee80211_proto.h
.In net80211/ieee80211_ioctl.h
.Ft int
.Fn ieee80211_cfgget "struct ieee80211com *ic" "u_long cmd" "void *data"
.Ft int
.Fn ieee80211_cfgset "struct ieee80211com *ic" "u_long cmd" "void *data"
.Ft int
.Fn ieee80211_ioctl "struct ieee80211com *ic" "u_long cmd" "void *data"
.Ft int
.Fo ieee80211_ioctl_sae
.Fa "struct ieee80211com *ic"
.Fa "u_long cmd"
.Fa "struct ieee80211req *ireq"
.Fa "uint32_t caps"
.Fa "int (*callback)(struct ieee80211com *, const struct ieee80211req_sae *)"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fn ieee80211_sae_configure_check "struct ieee80211com *ic" "uint32_t caps" "bool enable"
.Ft int
.Fn ieee80211_sta_request_validate "const struct ieee80211req_sta_mgmt *req"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These
functions are typically invoked by drivers in response to requests
for information or to change settings from the userland.
.Pp
.\"
The
.Fn ieee80211_cfgget
and
.Fn ieee80211_cfgset
functions implement a legacy interface for getting and setting 802.11
interface attributes respectively.
The interface is compatible with the RIDs implemented by the
.Xr wi 4
driver and used by the
.Xr wiconfig 8
utility.
.Pp
.\"
The
.Fn ieee80211_ioctl
function implements ioctls such as key management for wireless devices.
Ioctls related to the Ethernet layer also pass through here, but are
handed off to
.Fn ether_ioctl
when no match for
.Fa cmd
is found.
.\"
.Pp
.Fn ieee80211_ioctl_sae
handles the optional external SAE request ABI.
The driver supplies its probed capabilities and a chip callback.
A null callback returns
.Er EOPNOTSUPP .
GET returns capabilities without allocating or enabling SAE.
SET authorizes the caller, copies and validates the request, and invokes
only the supplied callback.
The helper clears the entire temporary request before freeing it on every
allocated path, including a partial copy fault or callback error.
Invalid request fields return
.Er EINVAL ;
unsupported SAE enablement returns
.Er EOPNOTSUPP .
Authorization and callback errors are returned unchanged.
.Pp
Call the helper from a sleepable context, before raising the network IPL.
The callback receives a kernel-owned request valid only until it returns.
It must copy any data needed by deferred work.
The chip driver owns state serialization, association lifetime checks,
and firmware commands.
Before changing configuration, the callback calls
.Fn ieee80211_sae_configure_check
with current capabilities and the validated enable flag under its state ownership.
This check runs after copyin, so a sleeping copy cannot authorize stale capabilities.
The capability argument to
.Fn ieee80211_ioctl_sae
is used only for GET.
Drivers that do not use external SAE need no callback or firmware dependency.
.Pp
.Fn ieee80211_sta_request_validate
checks the version, reserved field, payload bound, and input flags of an
already copied station request.
It returns zero or
.Er EINVAL .
The existing
.Va ic_sta_mgmt
callback remains the station management dispatch interface.
The common ioctl path also rejects GET operations submitted as SET.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wi 4 ,
.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
.Xr wiconfig 8 ,
.Xr ieee80211 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm ieee80211
series of functions first appeared in
.Nx 1.5 ,
and were later ported to
.Fx 4.6 .
